    <briefdescription>
<para>This class implements a matrix to keep track of the previous synchronization that occurred between each pair of streams in our pools. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>We record the largest event ID used to synchronized between two streams because synchronizing these two streams with an older event (with a lower ID) is implied by the previous synchronization, so it can be skipped thanks to stream-ordering of operations.</para>
<para>This is implemented as a hash table where keys are pairs of IDs. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
